# Paper 1 (MTEF) — CC BY 4.0

## 1. Zenodo record metadata

On the published record, choose **Edit** (metadata edits do not create a new
version or DOI). Under **Licenses**, remove whatever is there and select
**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International** (`CC-BY-4.0`). Under
**Access**, confirm **Open**. Save and **Publish** the metadata change.

## 2. Statement for the record's Description field

Paste at the end of the Zenodo description (plain text or HTML):

```
This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
© 2026 Jason Doffing. You may share and adapt this work for any purpose,
including commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the
license, and indicate if changes were made.
```

HTML form, if the description is HTML:

```html
<p>This work is licensed under a
<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)</a>.
&copy; 2026 Jason Doffing.</p>
```

## 3. Notice for the paper itself

Add to the front matter (title page footer or the line under the abstract) so
the PDF carries the license wherever it is copied. Adding it requires a new
file, which on Zenodo means a **new version** (the concept DOI stays the same;
the version gets its own DOI). If you would rather not cut a new version, the
record-level license in step 1 is sufficient on its own.

```
© 2026 Jason Doffing. This work is licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
```

## 4. Suggested citation line (for the record and the paper)

```
Doffing, J. (2026). <Paper 1 title>. Zenodo. https://doi.org/<Paper 1 DOI>
```

Fill in the title and DOI from the record.

## Notes

- Zenodo publishes the license as machine-readable metadata, so no LICENSE
  file needs to be uploaded alongside the PDF.
- The full legal code is in `../cc-by-4.0/LICENSE` if you want it attached to
  any mirror of the paper (jasondoffing.com, the Institute's Phase Space page).
- Assignment to the IP Vault at Step 2 does not change any of this: CC BY 4.0
  is irrevocable, and the new owner inherits the grant already made.
